Can we rewrite how {zei} works and postulate that the last part of words
glued together with {zei} determines its grammar?
Thus, {panpi zei coi} will become a vocative but {coi zei panpi} will be a
brivla as well as {broda zei brode zei panpi}?
This will eliminate at least one usage of {ze'ei}.

I'm not sure what {coi zei coi} could mean as a brivla and what would it be
its place structure.

